                              <pubPlace xml:id="pubPlace_b5e8fc4e">Copenhagen</pubPlace>
                           </imprint>
                           <title level="a" xml:id="title_8d0d09ea">Kirkekoncert</title>
                           <title level="j" xml:id="title_d6b380e3">Dagbladet</title>
                           <biblScope unit="issue" xml:id="biblScope_1970e6bc">95</biblScope>
                           <biblScope unit="page" xml:id="biblScope_f456c1c2">2</biblScope>
                        </bibl>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_476ef470">
                        <head xml:id="head_ac3a0f8b">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm138">Adolf Langsted at the request of Hartmann in December 1887, sent some information about the songs in the "Et Korstog. En religiøs-romantisk Digtning" (A Crusade. A Religious-Romantic Poem) which he found suited for music. He especially recommended "Korsfarersang", but pointed out that if the rhythm was too similar to "Dejlig er Jorden", there were also other possibilities. It was Langsted's wish that the songs should be ready in March, but Hartmann did not compose them until the summer of 1888.</p>
            </history>
